and have the reasoning source model generate up to 50 tokens, stopping at the first newline. The generated text is normalized (lowercase, strip articles, strip punctuation) and compared to the gold answer. Importantly, this protocol uses a different prompt format from the in-loop ReAct evaluation:

there is no Thought: cue, no turn-by-turn interleaving, and the agent is not asked to issue further searches. This is why the absolute EM rates in Table 4 are much lower than the in-loop PASS@(1, 5) values in Table 2: the cross-policy prompt is deliberately stripped to isolate the reasoning-only contribution. The value of the experiment is in the relative ordering across the four conditions, not the absolute numbers. Strategy diversity normalization. When counting unique query sequences per problem, lowercase each query, strip surrounding punctuation and whitespace, collapse internal whitespace, and then form the ordered tuple of normalized queries as the sequence key. Without this normalization, cosmetic variations such as trailing periods or capitalization differences would count as distinct strategies and inflate the novelty fraction; with it, the 3× diversity collapse of π SFT vs. π base is preserved, indicating that the effect is not a tokenization artifact.
